  "caption": "Synthetic: one-pass sketches need S*/N >= 0.25 (or never reach the exact centroid) at alpha in [0.75, 1.0]; S*/N <= 1e-2 at alpha in [0.0, 0.25, 0.5] for some N (best = Misra-Gries, S* ~ d_eff). Linear sketches (count-sketch, hashing, sparse JL) never reach the exact centroid at any S <= N here: dense noise collides into the signal. Real gene-pair tasks (20; PBMC3k K = 512\u202613,714, AIDA K = 512/2,048): log d_eff / log N = 0.23\u20130.74; measured best one-pass S*/N = 8.5e-08\u20133.9e-03 (all <= 1e-2). The most spread real task (AIDA hematopoietic stem cell (pairs), y = 0.74) sits next to the synthetic failure edge (y ~ 0.75) but still needs only S*/N = 1e-04: the isotropic-noise model is pessimistic, so d_eff alone does not predict failure. No real task falls where classical sketches fail.",
